1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,500
Little Moments.

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,437
The Almost-Perfect Picnic.

3
00:00:03,437 --> 00:00:05,990
Emma and I spread out a blanket in the park.

4
00:00:05,990 --> 00:00:10,927
Mom sets down the cooler, and Ben arrives carrying a bag of chips like it's a precious treasure.

5
00:00:10,927 --> 00:00:12,635
The weather is perfect.

6
00:00:12,635 --> 00:00:14,396
The food looks great.

7
00:00:14,396 --> 00:00:16,542
Then I open the pasta salad.

8
00:00:16,754 --> 00:00:18,204
Did anyone bring forks?

9
00:00:18,484 --> 00:00:20,111
I thought you had them.

10
00:00:20,282 --> 00:00:21,430
I brought plates.

11
00:00:21,430 --> 00:00:23,326
You said you were bringing the other stuff.

12
00:00:23,596 --> 00:00:25,173
I brought chips.

13
00:00:25,173 --> 00:00:27,236
I did my job beautifully.

14
00:00:27,508 --> 00:00:30,189
Let's see what we have before we go anywhere.

15
00:00:30,189 --> 00:00:33,825
Sandwiches, fruit, crackers, and that pasta salad.

16
00:00:34,108 --> 00:00:35,977
We can still make this work.

17
00:00:35,977 --> 00:00:38,050
We eat the sandwiches first.

18
00:00:38,050 --> 00:00:42,383
Emma passes around the fruit, and Ben opens his very important bag of chips.

19
00:00:42,383 --> 00:00:44,383
Nobody seems unhappy.

20
00:00:44,618 --> 00:00:46,370
The pasta can come home with us.

21
00:00:46,370 --> 00:00:49,349
It'll be an excellent second picnic on the kitchen table.

22
00:00:49,636 --> 00:00:50,942
Good plan.

23
00:00:50,942 --> 00:00:53,671
I'll keep it cold in the cooler until we get home.

24
00:00:53,956 --> 00:00:57,450
We watch a tiny dog trying to carry a stick twice its size.

25
00:00:57,450 --> 00:01:01,283
Ben puts a cracker next to his sandwich and says he's building a food castle.

26
00:01:01,514 --> 00:01:05,422
Next time, let's make one list and put our names beside the things we're bringing.

27
00:01:05,692 --> 00:01:07,644
Put me down for chips again.

28
00:01:07,644 --> 00:01:09,467
I'm experienced now.

29
00:01:09,748 --> 00:01:13,002
On the way home, I add forks to our next picnic list.

30
00:01:13,002 --> 00:01:17,356
Then I add a second line underneath: Check that someone actually packed the forks.

31
00:01:17,356 --> 00:01:19,669
That feels like an important detail.
